    "title_en": "First Measurement of Compton Scattering on $^3\\text{He}$ at HI$γ$S",
    "abstract_en": "The world's first Compton scattering measurements on a $^3$He target were performed to probe neutron electromagnetic polarizabilities. Differential cross sections were measured at laboratory angles of $40^\\circ$, $55^\\circ$, $90^\\circ$, $115^\\circ$, $150^\\circ$, using circularly polarized, quasi-monoenergetic photon beams at weighted mean energy values of 61.5 and 97.1 MeV from the High Intensity $γ$-ray Source at the Triangle Universities Nuclear Laboratory. Comparisons with chiral effective field theory show good agreement at 97.1 MeV but over-prediction at 61.5 MeV, motivating further theoretical development.",
